impíre(oim) ímpíre(oim) - A simple game with simple rules - if you lose, the world ends!

The game is played on a 4x4 grid:

After the start, the user must place some stones into the grid. Each move the player must choose one of three modes: they can place a stone into an empty square or move a stone (i.e. remove it from its current position and place it into an adjacent empty square.) The game ends when the grid is filled or no empty squares remain.

There is another rule: stones can be placed into lower parts of the grid only if the empty square (after the stone is placed there) is surrounded on all sides by stones - i.e. the player cannot make a mistake and place a stone into a square where it will fall down.

Usage: impíre(oim) [option] ...

Options:

-? - help

-h - print the version

-l - show the current level (default)

-n - do not show the grid (default)

-s - show the grid

-v - verbose mode

Examples:

impíre(oim) -n

impíre(oim) -s -l 3

impíre(oim) -v -s -l 2

impíre(oim) -h

