# Convert the current DPI to a tuple
current_dpi_tuple = tuple(dpi[0]) + (600,)

# Create a new metadata dictionary
metadata = image.info.copy()
metadata["dpi"] = current_dpi_tuple

# Overwrite the old DPI metadata with the new tuple
image.putmetadata(metadata)

# Save the image with the updated DPI
image.save("image_dpi_600.jpg")

Now the image should be the same size, but with a different DPI. You can verify this by opening the image in an image editor or by calculating the new physical size for the DPI. 

